WEBVTT

00:08.425 --> 00:09.843
Are you sure it's this way?

00:09.926 --> 00:11.970
Yes, we're almost there.

00:14.973 --> 00:16.099
Found him.

00:18.226 --> 00:19.436
Kanamori!

00:29.654 --> 00:31.531
You cut it down in the blink of an eye.

00:34.617 --> 00:37.537
Thank you very much, Sir Tokito!

00:37.620 --> 00:39.039
Kanamori!

00:39.581 --> 00:43.543
Young Kotetsu! I'm glad you're all right!

00:44.002 --> 00:46.713
To be honest,
I thought you were already dead.

00:46.796 --> 00:48.673
I thought the same.

00:48.757 --> 00:51.176
Are you the one called Kanamori?

00:52.677 --> 00:55.180
Tokito, he's Kanamori.

00:56.431 --> 00:58.516
Is my sword ready?

00:59.893 --> 01:00.977
Give it to me now.

01:01.061 --> 01:04.981
Oh, my! This is terribly chipped.

01:06.399 --> 01:08.109
That's why I came to the village.

01:08.735 --> 01:10.403
I understand.

01:11.196 --> 01:14.282
I'm finished with your sword.
I'm ready to give it to you.

01:15.116 --> 01:16.826
You're quick to understand.

01:17.285 --> 01:20.413
Aren't you glad? You should be grateful.

01:20.497 --> 01:25.126
Tanjiro asked me to prepare
a sword for you.

01:25.210 --> 01:28.129
And he wanted me to understand you.

01:29.422 --> 01:30.632
Tanjiro…

01:31.925 --> 01:33.176
Tanjiro did?

01:33.885 --> 01:37.972
So I looked up
who your swordsmith was and--

01:38.056 --> 01:42.060
Kanamori! We have to
get to Haganezuka quickly!

01:42.143 --> 01:43.728
If he's been attacked by demons…

01:43.812 --> 01:45.146
Now that you mention it!

01:45.230 --> 01:48.399
I'll take you to our manufacturing hut!

02:04.541 --> 02:07.502
Demon Slayer: Swordsmith Village Arc

03:21.200 --> 03:25.914
Episode 5: Bright Red Sword

03:26.915 --> 03:28.291
I'm worried about the village.

03:28.958 --> 03:34.172
We need you, a Hashira, to bring a sword
and help them as soon as possible.

03:35.215 --> 03:36.049
That hut!

03:36.132 --> 03:38.718
Good! No fish monsters here.

03:39.219 --> 03:41.054
I was working in that hut.

03:41.137 --> 03:44.015
There's a sword for you inside.

03:44.098 --> 03:47.435
Please take it and help the village chief!

03:48.228 --> 03:49.312
No, I can't.

03:50.313 --> 03:51.147
Why?

03:53.650 --> 03:54.901
Damn! That's annoying.

03:55.777 --> 03:56.903
It's here.

04:18.216 --> 04:21.219
I'm amazed you noticed.

04:24.472 --> 04:27.976
You are a Hashira, aren't you?

04:34.399 --> 04:35.400
UPPER

04:35.483 --> 04:38.319
Is this miserable shack
so important to you?

04:40.154 --> 04:43.783
I wonder what you are doing
sneaking around.

04:43.908 --> 04:46.327
UPPER
FIVE

04:47.287 --> 04:49.747
We're under attack! It's the demons!

04:49.831 --> 04:51.249
We're under attack!

04:51.749 --> 04:53.835
Protect every clan leader!

04:54.294 --> 04:56.337
Get the swords for the Hashiras!

04:56.421 --> 04:57.839
Get the village chief to safety!

05:05.805 --> 05:07.515
Tetsugoro!

05:07.598 --> 05:08.725
Be careful!

05:08.808 --> 05:11.769
These monsters' claws
are sharp like blades!

05:11.853 --> 05:14.522
Get inside the building!

05:15.440 --> 05:18.151
Don't! Fall back! Fall back!

05:28.453 --> 05:29.787
A Hashira has come!

05:29.871 --> 05:31.456
Sorry for being late!

05:31.539 --> 05:34.042
It's all right, everyone!
I will kill them all!

05:36.878 --> 05:38.713
-Amazing!
-She's fast!

05:38.796 --> 05:39.630
So strong!

05:40.131 --> 05:42.425
I almost forgot because she's so cute,

05:42.508 --> 05:45.094
a Hashira is really strong.

05:46.220 --> 05:49.098
Please… Please help the village chief!

06:06.491 --> 06:08.576
Chief!

06:15.041 --> 06:16.375
Chief…

06:19.462 --> 06:20.671
Chief!

06:21.547 --> 06:26.844
The corps members who had been stationed
to guard the village were killed easily.

06:27.386 --> 06:33.142
I can't let the Chief, the most skilled
person in the village, die as well.

06:35.061 --> 06:36.395
It's too big.

06:37.021 --> 06:40.441
My attacks are useless
against this monster.

06:40.525 --> 06:42.693
And it's so fast.

06:48.366 --> 06:50.326
It's better for you to stay put.

06:50.409 --> 06:52.912
I think you have internal injuries.

06:53.371 --> 06:55.748
Lady Kanroji!

06:57.291 --> 06:59.210
What's with her sword?

06:59.293 --> 07:02.130
Did Chief Tecchin forge it for her?

07:02.213 --> 07:05.591
I heard the rumors, but that's so bizarre.

07:09.220 --> 07:12.515
Love Breathing, First Form:

07:17.979 --> 07:20.398
Shivers of First Love.

07:25.570 --> 07:30.450
You know, my heart doesn't skip a beat
for those who hurt others.

07:41.919 --> 07:43.463
Chief Tecchin!

07:47.967 --> 07:49.802
Are you all right, Chief Tecchin?

07:50.511 --> 07:51.679
Hang in there!

07:53.222 --> 07:55.224
Chief Tecchin, can you hear me?

07:56.100 --> 08:01.731
I'm just happy to be hugged
by a sweet, young lady.

08:04.066 --> 08:07.111
Oh my, don't say that, Chief Tecchin.

08:07.195 --> 08:09.739
I fell on my head.

08:10.740 --> 08:12.408
Please hold my hand.

08:12.492 --> 08:15.411
Sorry! Are you all right?

08:15.495 --> 08:16.621
Don't interrupt!

08:17.413 --> 08:19.207
Thank goodness.

08:24.545 --> 08:25.713
What?

08:26.255 --> 08:27.632
What is this?

08:28.466 --> 08:29.884
What is this smell?

08:29.967 --> 08:33.721
You can't run away from me!

08:50.821 --> 08:51.822
Right.

08:52.323 --> 08:55.451
I was knocked unconscious
by that fan demon's attack.

08:55.993 --> 08:58.120
Nezuko must have woken up first.

09:06.212 --> 09:08.256
This is frustrating.

09:08.339 --> 09:10.299
Karaku, just blow it to bits!

09:10.383 --> 09:11.634
I will!

09:16.389 --> 09:19.058
You don't have to tell me!

09:22.853 --> 09:25.022
Think! Think!

09:25.565 --> 09:28.192
I must find a way to deal
a heavy blow to the enemy.

09:28.276 --> 09:30.945
An attack that slows down
their time to regenerate.

09:35.825 --> 09:38.869
Now, die, kiddo!

09:42.081 --> 09:44.000
This is your end!

09:52.967 --> 09:57.972
DEMON SLAYER: SWORDSMITH VILLAGE ARC

10:11.736 --> 10:14.488
With this, we can get a better view.

10:14.572 --> 10:18.784
Now they have nowhere to hide.

10:21.203 --> 10:23.247
Crap! She's trapped under the debris.

10:23.331 --> 10:26.751
Nezuko, don't worry. I won't leave you.

10:26.834 --> 10:29.629
Let go of my sword! I'll move the debris.

10:30.212 --> 10:32.923
Nezuko, stop it! You'll cut your fingers!

10:35.259 --> 10:37.762
You did a great job
razing the building to the ground.

10:38.596 --> 10:42.266
When this smoke clears,
it'll be their end.

10:44.769 --> 10:47.605
Nezuko, stop! Please stop it!

10:56.572 --> 11:00.785
Nice to meet you. You can call me Gyokko.

11:00.868 --> 11:03.913
Mind if I have a word before I kill you?

11:04.914 --> 11:06.415
Why are you two behind me?

11:06.499 --> 11:08.668
Because we're not safe on our own.

11:09.960 --> 11:16.384
I'd like to show the three of you
my creations tonight.

11:17.426 --> 11:21.180
Creations? What are you talking about?

11:22.640 --> 11:24.809
Here's the first one.

11:36.404 --> 11:40.157
I call this
"The Swordsmiths' Agonies of Death."

11:42.243 --> 11:44.120
Please take a good look!

11:44.203 --> 11:45.913
First of all, those hands!

11:45.996 --> 11:50.042
Dirty hands with thick calluses
of the swordsmiths!

11:50.126 --> 11:54.296
I put this work up first on purpose.

11:54.922 --> 11:57.299
Sir Kongoji… Tetsuo…

11:57.842 --> 12:00.719
Kanaike… Kotaro…

12:01.220 --> 12:02.680
Uncle Tetsuhiro…

12:03.180 --> 12:06.517
Yes! You both are right!

12:06.600 --> 12:13.190
This work incorporates
lavish details of five swordsmiths!

12:16.402 --> 12:19.822
I didn't expect you'd be so moved.

12:19.905 --> 12:25.327
These stabbed swords can
emphasize that they were smiths.

12:25.411 --> 12:31.667
I left the hyottoko masks on to convey
the lack of emotion and the absurdity.

12:31.750 --> 12:35.629
Of course, that's not all of it.

12:35.713 --> 12:37.965
And this is the best part.

12:38.048 --> 12:41.260
If I twist the sword here…

12:44.263 --> 12:46.765
Stop that!

12:52.396 --> 12:56.525
What do you think? Isn't it wonderful?

12:56.609 --> 12:59.904
A reenactment of their miseries!

12:59.987 --> 13:01.238
Hey.

13:01.322 --> 13:04.366
I've had enough of your shit, you bastard.

13:17.296 --> 13:20.216
I haven't finished explaining!

13:21.133 --> 13:23.677
Let me finish it first.

13:25.054 --> 13:27.556
Did he just travel between vases?

13:28.307 --> 13:29.517
I see.

13:30.017 --> 13:32.394
My pickiness is that vase's--

13:33.854 --> 13:35.773
I almost didn't feel anything.

13:39.902 --> 13:41.195
He got away again.

13:41.695 --> 13:42.947
He moves so fast.

13:43.906 --> 13:45.282
The next one is over there.

13:45.824 --> 13:47.618
The vase was already there
when I noticed it.

13:47.701 --> 13:52.081
How dare you cut my vase!

13:52.164 --> 13:55.876
That was a work of art!
You uncultured monkey!

13:56.877 --> 13:59.213
Where does the vase come from?

14:00.005 --> 14:03.884
A muscle-head like you couldn't

14:03.968 --> 14:07.638
possibly understand my work!

14:07.721 --> 14:09.265
But that's all right!

14:10.224 --> 14:16.021
But wait, if he's always running,
he's different from the splitting demon.

14:16.689 --> 14:18.983
He'll die if I behead him.

14:24.321 --> 14:27.157
Thousand Needle Fish Kill!

14:29.285 --> 14:30.202
Tokito!

14:37.167 --> 14:38.460
Young Kotetsu!

14:46.385 --> 14:47.595
Sir Tokito!

14:48.137 --> 14:49.930
You just get in my way, so go hide.

14:51.682 --> 14:52.766
I'm sorry.

14:53.475 --> 14:55.102
I…

15:04.028 --> 15:07.990
You look ridiculous with all those
needles sticking out of your body.

15:08.073 --> 15:09.700
How are you feeling?

15:09.783 --> 15:14.246
Has the poison begun
paralyzing your limbs?

15:14.330 --> 15:16.790
It is really ridiculous.

15:16.874 --> 15:22.296
You save worthless lives and then
lose yours in a worthless place.

15:22.379 --> 15:25.007
Your presence makes no difference.

15:27.301 --> 15:30.262
Your life is worthless.

15:31.722 --> 15:34.475
Who is that? I can't remember.

15:35.851 --> 15:38.437
I feel like someone once told me
the same thing.

15:39.480 --> 15:40.856
Who said that to me?

15:42.608 --> 15:44.944
It was summer. It was hot.

15:46.070 --> 15:47.321
The door was open.

15:48.238 --> 15:49.782
Was it because so hot?

15:49.865 --> 15:52.952
The cicadas were noisy even at night.

15:54.954 --> 15:59.249
But still, you're a Hashira, after all.

15:59.333 --> 16:02.753
I'm very excited to make
some artwork out of you!

16:04.713 --> 16:05.881
Shut up.

16:05.965 --> 16:08.217
It's your prattling that's worthless.

16:19.436 --> 16:22.898
Blood Demon Art: Water Prison Pot.

16:24.316 --> 16:28.404
Death by suffocation
is so elegant and beautiful.

16:28.487 --> 16:33.283
That chilly feeling when
you have a blade to your neck…

16:33.367 --> 16:35.869
What a nice feeling.

16:39.206 --> 16:40.916
It's no use. I can't cut it.

16:41.834 --> 16:45.879
I stopped your breathing technique,
the demon hunters' greatest weapon.

16:45.963 --> 16:51.844
I can't help but imagine how splendid
your writhing, contorted face is.

16:52.428 --> 16:56.515
Destroying the village will be
a great loss to the demon hunters.

16:57.266 --> 16:59.560
Once the demon hunters are weakened,

16:59.643 --> 17:02.688
Ubuyashiki's head will be next.

17:05.399 --> 17:06.316
Nezuko!

17:06.400 --> 17:08.652
Let go of my sword, Nezuko!

17:17.286 --> 17:20.247
My sword is burnt by Nezuko's blood.

17:22.249 --> 17:23.709
It's changing color.

17:25.502 --> 17:29.339
As the temperature rises,
my black sword is turning red.

17:30.340 --> 17:32.051
It's covered in her exploding blood.

17:32.676 --> 17:33.761
This is…

17:37.473 --> 17:38.932
Exploding Blood Blade.

17:40.768 --> 17:42.853
It's turning red.

17:43.479 --> 17:47.941
Mister Samurai, so your sword
turns red only when you fight.

17:48.859 --> 17:50.027
What?

17:50.110 --> 17:52.780
Why is that? So mysterious.

17:53.238 --> 17:56.075
Usually, it's deep black like obsidian.

17:56.784 --> 17:57.785
Who was she?

17:57.868 --> 18:00.162
It's very pretty.

18:00.829 --> 18:01.705
Who was she really?

18:03.207 --> 18:06.293
This must be an inherited memory.

18:07.503 --> 18:11.590
She probably meant the swordsman
with the earrings by "Mister Samurai."

18:12.341 --> 18:15.511
Was his sword deep black in color?

18:16.261 --> 18:17.554
A black blade like mine.

18:18.097 --> 18:20.724
And now, my sword turned red as well.

18:21.266 --> 18:22.476
The color changed.

18:23.936 --> 18:27.272
It turned red thanks to the power
of Nezuko's blood.

18:27.356 --> 18:30.484
I'm sure it's a different
from that swordsman,

18:30.901 --> 18:33.529
but right now, my sword is like his.

18:34.613 --> 18:38.534
Even if I get stronger, so do the demons.

18:39.493 --> 18:42.704
A human body will get
injured and battered easily.

18:44.081 --> 18:49.253
But each time, somebody helps and
saves me so I can hold on to my life.

18:50.420 --> 18:51.755
I have to repay them.

18:53.215 --> 18:55.509
The hopes and feelings of everyone

18:55.884 --> 18:58.428
who lent their strength to me
are the same.

18:59.346 --> 19:00.848
It's to defeat the demons.

19:01.849 --> 19:03.767
It's to protect human lives.

19:09.815 --> 19:12.109
I have to answer their calls!

19:14.778 --> 19:17.614
You can't beat me with cheap tricks.

19:17.698 --> 19:20.784
It won't hurt or even itch if you cut me!

19:23.328 --> 19:25.914
A burning, bright red blade…

19:27.124 --> 19:28.792
Based on Lord Muzan's memory,

19:30.419 --> 19:36.258
it belonged to the swordsman who cornered
and almost severed Lord Muzan's head.

19:40.888 --> 19:42.806
Its image is overlapping.

19:46.894 --> 19:48.395
Hinokami Kagura:

19:49.188 --> 19:50.564
Dragon Sun Halo…

20:11.168 --> 20:12.419
Head Dance!

20:31.730 --> 20:35.150
I have been thinking about
that one strike.

20:36.652 --> 20:40.364
The reason why that strike had
the power to sever Gyutaro's head.

20:42.616 --> 20:45.118
The sensation of that moment,
my breathing,

20:45.494 --> 20:47.079
and the way I used my strength…

20:47.663 --> 20:51.500
My whole body felt like it was on fire,
and my forehead as well.

20:53.377 --> 20:54.336
I get it now.

20:54.962 --> 20:56.004
I can do this.

20:57.089 --> 20:58.090
Only one more.

20:58.674 --> 21:01.009
All four heads must be cut
at the same time.

21:01.093 --> 21:02.386
Where's the last one?

21:05.472 --> 21:07.307
Genya! He's okay.

21:09.351 --> 21:11.270
He cut the head of the fourth one.

21:11.770 --> 21:13.021
Good! He did it!

21:13.480 --> 21:15.983
Was it at the same time? If he did…

21:16.775 --> 21:17.693
Genya!

21:26.493 --> 21:27.369
Is that Genya?

21:27.869 --> 21:30.038
Why does he look like that?

21:31.331 --> 21:32.374
He's just like…

21:33.917 --> 21:35.168
Just like…

23:06.051 --> 23:07.052
DEMON SLAYER: SWORDSMITH VILLAGE ARC
NO. 5

23:07.886 --> 23:11.098
How do you sheath your sword?

23:11.181 --> 23:12.849
Well, if you ask how…

23:12.933 --> 23:15.060
Poisonous potato.

23:19.648 --> 23:21.608
No, that was a joke.

23:25.320 --> 23:27.114
That's amazing!

23:28.782 --> 23:31.326
Is it really that amazing?

23:31.409 --> 23:34.830
Yes, it is!
I expect nothing less from you!

23:34.913 --> 23:36.498
Is that so?

23:36.581 --> 23:38.834
Okay, I'll show you one more time.

23:42.546 --> 23:44.339
You're incredible, Kanroji!

23:44.422 --> 23:45.966
Really?

23:46.049 --> 23:49.010
Well, one more time, then.

23:49.094 --> 23:51.304
It's just for you, Tanjiro.

23:51.388 --> 23:52.639
But before that…

23:52.722 --> 23:55.892
Next up on Episode 6:
"Aren't You Going to be a Hashira?"

23:57.936 --> 23:59.646
You're really awesome!

23:59.896 --> 24:00.981
TO BE CONTINUED
